    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0505" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.61/285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)<anchor n="34" xml:id="d475-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-25T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1507. It is the belief of the Department that to a large extent the difficulty in
                    the situation regarding Poland is due to the failure of the Allied and
                    Associated Powers to see the problem from the same point of view and to reach a
                    measure of agreement regarding the real objective sufficient to allow their
                    recommendations to coincide. In case the Conference of Ambassadors takes up the
                    subject, you can express the belief of this Government in the desirability of as
                    complete agreement as possible in any recommendation that the Conference may
                    make at this juncture to Poland. In expressing this view you may be assured that
                    you are giving a correct interpretation of the ideas of this Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d475-f1" n="34" type="source" xml:id="d475-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted on the same date to the Minister in Poland (no. 402).</p>
